# Copy to frontend/.env.local for a build where the frontend and backend
# don't share a host. Not required for local dev -- see README's Setup
# section -- and only takes effect at build time (Vite bakes it into the
# bundle), not at runtime.

# Base URL of the deployed backend, e.g. https://api.example.com (no
# trailing slash). Unset means "assume the backend is on this same
# hostname, port 8000" -- true for local dev and single-host deploys,
# not true when the frontend is deployed separately (e.g. Vercel) from
# the backend (e.g. Railway/Render/Fly.io). See README's Deploy section.
VITE_API_BASE_URL=
